Package: ycpy
Version: 1.0.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, ibus (>= 1.5)
Recommends: fonts-noto-cjk
Maintainer: YingRongjun <52067369@qq.com>
Description: Yingche Pinyin - Pinyin input method for IBus (written in Python)
 Supports full pinyin, initial-letter shorthand, fuzzy typo tolerance,
 associative candidates, word-frequency learning and whole-sentence
 segmentation. Pure Python: no compiler and no extra Python packages
 are required.
 .
 The dictionaries are all built from public corpora and statistics
 (jieba word frequencies, Jun Da's Modern Chinese Character Frequency
 List, Unicode Unihan). No word list is hand-written. See
 /usr/share/doc/ycpy/CREDITS.md for sources and licences.
 .
 The ibus component is installed under /usr/share/ibus/component, so
 ibus-daemon picks it up on its next start - no logout/login needed.
 ycpy shows up in the GNOME input source list right away.
 .
 Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3 or later. The
 dictionaries themselves carry their own upstream licences - the
 whole-sentence frequency table comes from rime-frost (GPL-3.0),
 which is why the project is GPL-3.0-or-later; see
 /usr/share/doc/ycpy/CREDITS.md for the full audit.
 Chinese description: /usr/share/doc/ycpy/copyright and the AppStream
 metadata /usr/share/metainfo/ycpy.metainfo.xml
